    "recommendations": "• Remove or thin the dense tree clusters closest to the structure to create more open space between the trees and the building.\n• Trim branches from trees that hang directly over or within a few feet of the roof and walls.\n• Cut back shrubs and low plants that are growing against or touching the outside walls of the structure.\n• Thin the mixed vegetation surrounding the structure to break up the continuous ring of plants and trees pressing close to the building.\n• Remove dead or dry material from within the scattered shrubs near the structure.\n• Keep the single access route clear of overhanging branches and encroaching vegetation along both sides so vehicles can pass through without obstruction.\n• Mark the driveway entry clearly so it remains visible to responding vehicles approaching under low visibility conditions.\n• Maintain the open green space by keeping it mowed or grazed short, particularly in areas adjacent to the structure.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure to widen the open areas between the tree canopy and the building walls."
